The terminal core under src/src/term/ and the composer editor in
src/src/tui/editor.lisp are derived from cl-tuition, Anthony Green's
Common Lisp port of charmbracelet's bubbletea, bubbles and lipgloss:

    https://github.com/atgreen/cl-tuition
    upstream 6f69592 (v2.3.0), plus the nodecode fork's commits 22b1dc2
    (terminal capabilities: clipboard, OSC 8, kitty graphics, kitty
    keyboard, input and render correctness) and ff6e5e1 (the mode
    lifecycle never erases), and its final 234 lines (readline chords,
    the soft-wrap visual cursor step, LF as Ctrl+J, ESC ESC and ESC + C0
    decoding), archived as the tag nodecode-absorbed.

They are reduced, not vendored: message.lisp, width.lisp, screen.lisp (their cells.lisp),
terminal.lisp, input.lisp, image.lisp and render.lisp carry the fork's
mechanism with every path the shells never reach removed; program.lisp
and editor.lisp are rewritten to the shape the shells run. Each derived
file keeps its SPDX header and copyright line.

